WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.321 --> 00:00:16.722
Scrooge opened his eyes.

2
00:00:18.383 --> 00:00:21.204
Belle and her husband were now sitting together by the fireplace.

3
00:00:22.884 --> 00:00:26.006
The children were quieter now, playing with their new toys.

4
00:00:26.026 --> 00:00:31.488
"Belle," her husband said, turning toward her with a smile.

5
00:00:32.412 --> 00:00:34.973
"I saw an old friend of yours this afternoon."

6
00:00:34.993 --> 00:00:37.193
"Who was it?"

7
00:00:37.674 --> 00:00:38.314
she asked.

8
00:00:38.334 --> 00:00:41.335
"Guess!" he said.

9
00:00:41.355 --> 00:00:45.356
"I have no idea!"

10
00:00:45.536 --> 00:00:46.496
she said with a laugh.

11
00:00:47.736 --> 00:00:49.117
Then her eyes widened.

12
00:00:49.137 --> 00:00:51.277
"I know who it was!

13
00:00:52.738 --> 00:00:53.938
Mr. Scrooge!"

14
00:00:56.339 --> 00:01:00.180
"Mr. Scrooge it was," Her husband grinned.

15
00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:04.922
"I passed by the window of his office earlier this evening.

16
00:01:06.944 --> 00:01:11.647
Unlike all the other offices on the street, his building wasn't shuttered for the holiday.

17
00:01:12.928 --> 00:01:16.250
And, of course, there was a candle burning inside."

18
00:01:19.373 --> 00:01:22.295
His smile faded, and he shook his head sadly.

19
00:01:22.315 --> 00:01:26.518
"I hear his partner, Jacob Marley, lies near death.

20
00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:30.420
And yet Mr.

21
00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:35.983
Scrooge sat there at work, just as he did when his sister was dying several years ago.

22
00:01:37.264 --> 00:01:39.685
Soon he'll be quite alone in the world, won't he?

23
00:01:40.726 --> 00:01:41.426
By now, Mr.

24
00:01:41.446 --> 00:01:45.248
Marley must be the only person who willingly spends time with him."

25
00:01:45.268 --> 00:01:49.651
"I suppose so," Belle said softly.

26
00:01:49.671 --> 00:01:54.713
"I do pity him, even after all the pain he caused me long ago."

27
00:01:57.015 --> 00:01:59.176
"Spirit!" Scrooge cried.

28
00:01:59.952 --> 00:02:01.774
"I can't bear watching Belle.

29
00:02:02.875 --> 00:02:05.296
Take me home and haunt me no more."

30
00:02:07.378 --> 00:02:09.760
Scrooge turned, lunging toward the ghost.

31
00:02:10.481 --> 00:02:14.444
But just before he reached it, he fell to the floor in a deep sleep.

32
00:02:18.507 --> 00:02:21.169
When Scrooge awoke, he was back in his own bed.

33
00:02:22.350 --> 00:02:24.532
He sat up and looked around nervously.

34
00:02:25.716 --> 00:02:32.520
"Come, spirit number two, if you're still planning a visit," he said in a shaky voice.

35
00:02:32.540 --> 00:02:37.123
"I just want to get this strange business over with."

36
00:02:38.504 --> 00:02:39.504
But nothing came.

37
00:02:42.066 --> 00:02:43.447
A quarter of an hour passed.

38
00:02:44.948 --> 00:02:48.009
Scrooge got up and paced anxiously around his room.

39
00:02:51.612 --> 00:02:56.074
Finally he noticed a red glow coming from beneath his bedroom door.

40
00:02:59.996 --> 00:03:02.878
no normal firelight," Scrooge thought.

41
00:03:03.618 --> 00:03:05.099
He put his hand on the doorknob.

42
00:03:05.780 --> 00:03:10.082
A strange, deep voice called out, "Ebenezer Scrooge!

43
00:03:10.182 --> 00:03:11.743
Please enter."

44
00:03:13.664 --> 00:03:15.685
Scrooge trembled but obeyed.

45
00:03:18.587 --> 00:03:22.845
He stepped into his sitting room, though it didn't look much like his sitting room anymore.

46
00:03:24.485 --> 00:03:29.287
The walls and ceiling were hung with so many branches and vines that it looked like a forest

47
00:03:29.327 --> 00:03:37.729
grove. A mighty blaze was burning in the fireplace, far larger and hotter than any fire that Scrooge

48
00:03:37.749 --> 00:03:38.329
had ever built.

49
00:03:39.549 --> 00:03:43.110
When Scrooge stepped forward, his slipper hit something on the floor.

50
00:03:44.491 --> 00:03:48.052
Glancing down, he was surprised to see items from a feast.

51
00:03:49.100 --> 00:03:52.642
There were roasted turkeys and geese and wreaths of sausages.

52
00:03:54.703 --> 00:03:57.224
There were plum puddings and barrels of oysters.

53
00:03:59.725 --> 00:04:02.786
He saw red apples as well as enormous bowls of punch.

54
00:04:04.787 --> 00:04:10.270
Right in the middle of all that food sat a jolly giant, grinning as he held a glowing

55
00:04:10.330 --> 00:04:13.091
torch. "Come in!"

56
00:04:13.711 --> 00:04:14.612
the spirit said.

57
00:04:17.424 --> 00:04:19.766
"I am the Ghost of Christmas Present.

58
00:04:20.547 --> 00:04:21.888
Look at me!"

59
00:04:23.549 --> 00:04:26.511
His voice was friendly, and so was his expression.

60
00:04:28.152 --> 00:04:33.436
He wore a simple green robe bordered with white fur, and his feet were bare.

61
00:04:35.077 --> 00:04:39.840
Upon his mass of dark brown curls sat a holly wreath decorated with icicles.

62
00:04:42.022 --> 00:04:47.065
"Spirit," Scrooge said humbly, "take me wherever you like.

63
00:04:47.986 --> 00:04:51.949
I have already learned some lessons tonight, and I'm ready for more."

64
00:04:55.211 --> 00:04:56.312
The spirit chuckled.

65
00:04:56.332 --> 00:04:58.814
"Touch my robe."

66
00:05:00.735 --> 00:05:04.217
Scrooge did as he was told, grabbing onto the edge of the garment.

67
00:05:06.759 --> 00:05:09.681
Suddenly all the food and greenery disappeared.

68
00:05:10.462 --> 00:05:13.064
So did the room, the fire, and the night.

69
00:05:14.760 --> 00:05:17.502
They were standing on a city street on Christmas morning.

70
00:05:19.504 --> 00:05:25.729
It had snowed heavily, and everywhere Scrooge looked, people were out shoveling their stoops and rooftops.

71
00:05:25.749 --> 00:05:31.794
"It must be bitterly cold out," Scrooge said.

72
00:05:33.195 --> 00:05:37.258
Even though he couldn't feel the weather, he could see the shovelers' red noses and cheeks.

73
00:05:39.240 --> 00:05:44.384
The wind was blowing drifts of snow around, and icicles dripped from every surface.

74
00:05:46.164 --> 00:05:48.785
"Yes, it's very cold," the ghost said.

75
00:05:48.805 --> 00:05:54.768
"But these people all seem so cheerful," Scrooge said.

76
00:05:54.788 --> 00:05:56.828
"Just look at them."

77
00:05:58.369 --> 00:06:03.031
He watched as a young man tossed a snowball from one rooftop toward another rooftop.

78
00:06:04.071 --> 00:06:07.713
It hit another young man, who shouted with glee and threw one back.

79
00:06:09.613 --> 00:06:11.994
Several women were sweeping a stoop nearby.

80
00:06:13.655 --> 00:06:15.536
One started humming a festive tune.

81
00:06:17.416 --> 00:06:20.059
Soon all of them were singing a carol while they worked.

82
00:06:22.542 --> 00:06:25.685
Scrooge shook his head in wonder at the people's joy.

83
00:06:25.705 --> 00:06:28.608
"Why are they so happy?"

84
00:06:29.109 --> 00:06:29.590
he thought.

85
00:06:29.610 --> 00:06:32.373
"I don't understand any of this."

86
00:06:33.934 --> 00:06:38.759
But before he could ask the spirit about it, the ghost swept him away to another place.
